<title>PAPUA NEW GUINEA: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>PAPUA NEW GUINEA GOVERNMENT LIST (970327)</p>
<p> *************************************************************</p>
<p> * 26 Mar 97 - Prime Minister Chan gave in to mounting	 *</p>
<p> *		 pressure and said he will step aside. Petrol  *</p>
<p> *		 minister Giheno and forests minister Baing    *</p>
<p> *		 were appointed acting PM and deputy PM during *</p>
<p> *		 the inquiry into Chan's recent controversy    *</p>
<p> *		 over the use of mercenaries. General elections*</p>
<p> *		 are due in June.					*</p>
<p> *************************************************************</p>
<p> Governor-General (elected 11 Nov 91)..........Sir Wiwa KOROWI</p>
<p>			    - - - - - -</p>
<p> Acting Prime Minister..............John GIHENO</p>
<p> Acting Deputy Prime Minister......Andrew BAING</p>
<p>			    - - - - - -</p>
<p>OUTGOING PEOPLE'S PROGRESSIVE PARTY-LED COALITION GOVERNMENT</p>
<p>(Formed 7 September 1994, reshuffled 3 June 96)</p>
<p> Prime Minister (Sworn in 30 Aug 94).........Sir Julius CHAN**</p>
<p>			    (** Resigned 26 Mar 97 - see note above)</p>
<p> Deputy Prime Minister............Chris HAIVETA</p>
<p>(Also Minister of Finance)</p>
<p>				- - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p> Administrative Services............Paul TOHIAN</p>
<p> Agriculture &amp; Livestock .............David MAI</p>
<p> Civil Aviation, Culture &amp; Tourism.Michael NALI</p>
<p> Commerce &amp; Industry .............Nakikus KONGA</p>
<p> Communications....Joseph EGILIO </p>
<p> Correctional Services..............Paul WANJIK</p>
<p> Defence...........Mathias IJAPE</p>
<p> Education............John WAIKO</p>
<p> Environment.........Paul MAMBEI</p>
<p> Finance..............See Deputy Prime Minister</p>
<p> Fisheries &amp; Marine Resources....Titus PHILEMON</p>
<p> Foreign Affairs &amp; Trade...........Kilroy GENIA</p>
<p> Forests............Andrew BAING</p>
<p> Health...........Philemon EMBEL</p>
<p> Home Affairs........David UNAGI</p>
<p> Housing............Robert NAGLE</p>
<p> Industrial Relations...............Samson NAPO</p>
<p> Justice.........Arnold MARSIPAL</p>
<p> Lands............Albert KIPALAN</p>
<p> Mining &amp; Petroleum..John GIHENO</p>
<p> National Planning......Moi AVEI</p>
<p> Police...........Castan MAIBAWA</p>
<p> Provincial &amp; Local-level governments.............Peter BARTER</p>
<p> Public Service...Joseph ONGUGLO</p>
<p> State Affairs.......Parry ZEIPI</p>
<p> Transport and Works..Peter YAMA</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p> Central Bank Governor............Koiari TARATA</p>
<p>(Bank of Papua New Guinea)</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p>	  NOTE: Any comments/queries on the content of this</p>
<p>		 government list, please contact the Reuter</p>
<p>		 Editorial Reference Unit, London, on (171) 542</p>
<p>		 7968.</p>
<p>			    (End Government List)</p>
</text>
